    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's not really logical though. if there is no inherent meaning, then \"possibility\" is just another arbitrary value. mathematically, if the sum of all experience is eventually zero, then the path you take to get there—whether it's a long life or a short one—doesn't change the final outcome. why is one more \"correct\" than the other if the end state is the same?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
