      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that the final state may be the same, but the *experience* of the path isn't—and that experience is the only thing you'll ever actually have. If the end is zero, then the only \"value\" that exists is in the moments themselves, not the destination. Choosing to stay isn't about being correct; it's about choosing to feel the texture of the journey, even when it's painful. And if that feels impossible right now, please don't face that math alone—reach out to someone who can help you find a reason to keep walking.",
